WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.290
For a hundred years the Astragius galaxy
had been split by war.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.460
I was ordered into an operation
whose details were kept from me.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.670
There, my destiny was changed
the moment I saw her.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.170
She was apparently the military's greatest secret.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.460
Since deserting the army, my wanderings
had brought me to the city of Uoodo.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:05.250
But, for a man like me
who only knows how to fight...

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.960
combat in this city was something
I could not avoid.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.920
And within the battle, I met her once more.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.330
She's deeply tied to my destiny.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.000
But what sort of destiny is it?

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Counterattack

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.750
I assume you've already heard
that Chirico's still alive.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.500
If worse comes to worse,
we'll be sending you out again.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.580
In that event, don't show any mercy. Kill him.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.460
Show us the extent of a Perfect Soldier's power.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.630
No.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.460
What did you say?

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.580
I said no!

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.290
Proto One!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.130
I don't believe it!
A Perfect Soldier, defying orders!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.880
Let's go, old man!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.540
Any time you're ready. The mission disk's all set.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.960
Turn the rabbit loose, old man!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.000
Gotcha!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.330
Chirico, do not try to resist!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.630
Chirico, do not try to resist!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.040
Resistance is useless!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.880
All paths of escape have been blocked!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.460
Throw down your gun
and surrender and you will live!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.290
Here he comes!

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.830
Chirico, do not try to resist!

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.000
Look! His left shoulder!

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.330
A Red Shoulder!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.420
He's a Red Shoulder?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.290
Did we get him?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.460
We must have.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.630
That wasn't so tough.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.420
May have been a Red Shoulder,
but there was only one of him.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.080
Guess so.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.540
I dunno. It doesn't feel right.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.250
That he was that easy to kill?

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.380
He's behind us! Turn around!

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.750
Back up!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.960
Over there! Forward!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.380
It's coming this way!

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.040
Okay, that's ten minutes.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.290
Let's go.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.080
That's a Red Shoulder for you. Amazing to see.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.540
Halt!

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:08.790
Heads up! Present for you!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.710
It's Chirico's gang! Contact headquarters!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.420
The police seem serious this time.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.750
They're trying to finish him off once and for all.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.670
But how could he have escaped from that fire?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:55.630
And then survive that mountain of weaponry
at the Battling stadium?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.500
Looks like we'll get no sleep tonight.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.330
Sir!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.420
I don't like doing this without
permission from headquarters.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.210
Getting permission is beside the point.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.630
The question is whether or not this PS
is functioning properly.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:17.170
Emergency message, sir.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.420
I'm listening.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.750
Trouble, sir.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.460
Chirico's broken out of the stadium
and has entered the city.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.630
What? Where's he headed?

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.960
On a direct course for police headquarters.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.170
Buy us one hour!

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.000
Do whatever it takes to slow him down!

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.170
Roger!

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.460
Things have gotten completely out of control.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.630
We have one hour.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.250
It'll have to be enough!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.080
Then let's begin.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.750
Nothing physically abnormal showing up.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.830
The problem's probably in her memory.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.630
It's numerically coded for retrieval,
but it'll take a while to pull out.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.290
All right, check Saturday, from three weeks ago.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.500
Time index?

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.130
Between three and five o'clock.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:06.380
Yes, sir. Understood.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.750
Three weeks ago?

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.000
The day Chirico broke into the armory.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:17.540
She denies it, but I think something
happened in her bathing room.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.210
We have to ascertain just what the truth is.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.630
Borough, I don't know what you're thinking,

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.630
but even if the Prototype did
encounter Chirico there

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.130
that's no reason for her to start defying us.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:36.630
Our conditioning to make her a battle-ready PS
should have implanted loyalty into her.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.000
Under normal circumstances, yes.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:46.000
But what if something else were to be
accidently implanted into her consciousness

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.290
before our conditioning began?

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.040
And what if that something...

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.790
...was Chirico?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.830
It's possible.

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.920
I believe Chirico was the first person
the Prototype ever saw.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.420
You may be right.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.380
It should be up soon.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.170
I have the memories for the sixth of May.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.130
Right here.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.290
Getting a visual.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.670
That's...!

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.000
Is it?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.500
Just as I thought!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:28.000
All right, now trace back to her
birthdate memory number.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:28.960
Yes, sir!

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.000
If my theory's correct, we have a major problem.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.040
I have the key number.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.540
This is the instant of birth.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.670
All right, now check before that!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.000
There shouldn't be anything
before the key number.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.830
Never mind, just check it.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:54.710
Yes, sir.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.790
What's wrong? I don't see anything.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:20.750
Right. Her memory's a void.
What do you expect to see?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.500
Don't panic.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.880
No, stop. We don't have time.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.250
What?

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:29.130
I'm reading a memory before
the birthdate number!

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:32.290
What's wrong?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.880
We're seeing the same thing that she is.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.500
"That she is?"

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.670
What is she seeing?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.420
Try to clear the image.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:43.210
Yes, sir.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.380
We can see it.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.630
Looks like a person.

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:54.040
We need it clearer!

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.250
I'll try.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:00.040
That's...!

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.500
Chirico! That has to be him!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.130
She's linked Chirico to her own birth.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:09.750
He was the first thing to be exposed to
a completely blank mind.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.710
Before her PS conditioning had even begun.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:18.000
You're saying Chirico exists as
an integral part of her consiousness?

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.170
I can't draw any conclusions,
but that seems to be the case.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.380
I don't believe this!

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:29.290
As long as she has this latent memory of him,
she's useless as a Perfect Soldier!

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.750
You god damned defect!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.580
Chief! This isn't a total loss!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.670
But...!

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:39.040
The Prototype's value as a weapon
remains unchanged.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.290
If we kill her here,
everything we've worked for will be wasted!

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.290
There's still a way to use her.

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.290
So please, just calm down.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.670
Chirico's reached sector 21.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.040
We need your orders, sir.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:36.460
Okay!

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.580
He got away! Contact sector 22!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.920
Chirico's turned towards the main street!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.330
Come around after him!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.500
Okay, what's his current location?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.670
He's run into the third building on the left.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.960
All right, get two armored cars after him.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.920
Looks like the police can't handle Chirico.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:38.040
True, but he'll be running out of ammo soon.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:40.580
And that should even the odds.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.330
This should be quite interesting.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.330
Only one cartridge left.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.540
Are we awake now?

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.000
So, how do you feel?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
You're all set to sortie.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.500
Now get going!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.130
No!

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.670
You dare to defy us?

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.960
There, there.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.460
What's wrong?

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.500
Why are you afraid to fight Chirico?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:15.420
I don't know why. All I know is that I can't.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:19.170
Then how about this:
you don't have to kill Chirico.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:23.080
All you have to do is disable his AT.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.420
We promise we won't kill him, either.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.000
Do you mean that?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.580
An impressive sight, the Brutish Dog.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.250
This should rip Chirico's Scopedog apart.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.330
This isn't something just anyone could handle.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.790
You alone can pilot this.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:53.000
Now go!

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.380
But don't forget what we've taught you!

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:02.210
About what being a Perfect Soldier means!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.790
Chirico's broken our defense line
and is headed for HQ.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:29.210
Scramble every armored car and chopper
you have to defend it!

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:32.630
Stop him! Kill that bastard!

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:43.380
Right! There!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.540
Fourteen armored cars... All destroyed!

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.580
Damn it! They got the compressor!

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.000
Chirico, do you read me?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.290
Where are you? Gotho!

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.460
Behind you, about 50 meters below.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.460
Watch it.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.710
You've still got two or three choppers hunting you.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:30.000
I can't move. Can you help me
get down there to you?

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:31.170
I gotcha.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.920
C'mon, spread this thing out.
We have to catch Chirico.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.330
Gotcha!
Okay, here we go.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.170
Okay!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:51.710
Chirico, can't you fall a little softer?

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.710
Sorry.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.290
I won't stop now that I've come this far.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.540
C'mon, the cops are right in front of us!

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:01.130
She's all charged up. Let 'em have it!

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:04.000
Nothing's gonna split us up now.

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:47.630
Damn!

00:18:58.790 --> 00:18:59.790
There you are.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.710
Hey what do we do?

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:23.420
There's nothing we can do.
We'll have to pull back for now.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:28.380
Stop the elevator!

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.580
Chirico's broken in! Chirico's broken in!

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:37.380
Where is he?

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:39.880
We don't know! Just get out of here!

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.880
Like hell I will! And just let him have this place?

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:46.420
We can come back once the
Prototype's settled things.

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:47.880
I suppose we have no choice.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.710
Chief! There you are!

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.630
Follow me!

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:52.330
Sir!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:58.920
Borough!

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.710
Hurry!

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:06.580
Today we end this!

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:03.130
Police headquarters has been occupied.

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:06.210
I believe the Prototype has been
captured by Chirico.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.580
So, Chirico wins.

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:14.000
No matter what the police try now,
Chirico will escape.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.460
Both he and the Prototype!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.000
The guy's a monster.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.670
I never thought it would turn out like this.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.380
Dispatch an emergency communique
to Gen. Battentain.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:26.880
With a formal request for troop deployment.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:38.750
We meet again.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:42.250
It's always just the two of us, alone.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:49.670
We're the only ones in this building now.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.170
Please, untie me. I won't resist.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:59.040
I doubt that rope could stop you
if you wanted to.

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:12.080
Are you going to kill me?

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:20.040
What's your name?

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:21.960
Proto One.

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:24.460
That isn't a name.

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:30.330
Proto One is all I've ever been called.

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:38.290
The woman who had changed my destiny
was no longer an enemy.

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.080
I couldn't shake the feeling that I was
sinking deeper and deeper into quicksand.

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:45.250
But at the same time, I felt something amazing.

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:51.420
Never before in my life had I
wanted so much to keep on living.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.210 --> 00:23:02.330
The Hundred Years War. Lido. The Prototype.
Chirico. Uoodo. Perfect Soldiers.

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:04.460
Worked by the hands of God,

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:07.330
the shuttle of destiny flies and weaves
these tangled threads together.

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:11.500
But what is the design He weaves
into the Astragius galaxy?

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:15.500
Drawn upon this great tapestry,
a moment of spectacular drama.

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:19.080
And in that moment,
Chirico calls out a name: Fyana.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:24.290
Bonds

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:21.420
Next time, "Bonds"

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:23.710
Soon, the casting will be complete.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
